# Trivy ignore list — CONTAINER IMAGE scan only.
#
# Deliberately separate from `.trivyignore`, which governs the filesystem scan
# of this repository's own dependency tree. The two scan different things and
# must not share suppressions: a CVE that is unfixable inside a vendored
# third-party binary is not the same as one in our lockfile, and suppressing it
# in the shared file would switch off the regression detection the filesystem
# gate exists to provide.
#
# Every entry here needs an `SD-*` row in docs/AUDIT_DEBT.md, same rule as the
# other file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESOLVED — kept as a note, not a suppression.
#
# This file previously suppressed three HIGH findings vendored inside the pnpm
# distribution that ships in the backend runtime image:
#
#   CVE-2026-69152  brace-expansion 2.1.2  fixed in 2.1.4
#   CVE-2026-69192  ip-address 10.2.0      fixed in 10.3.1
#   CVE-2026-55697  pnpm 10.34.5           fixed in 11.5.3
#
# All three are cleared by the pnpm 10.34.5 -> 11.20.0 upgrade, and the fix is
# stronger than a version bump: pnpm 11 vendors 23 packages where 10.34.5
# vendored 80, and `brace-expansion` and `ip-address` are not among them at all.
# Verified directly against both corepack caches — the same tree the image scan
# reads — rather than inferred from release notes:
#
#   pnpm 10.34.5: brace-expansion dirs=1  ip-address dirs=1  vendored pkgs=80
#   pnpm 11.20.0: brace-expansion dirs=0  ip-address dirs=0  vendored pkgs=23
#
# Recorded as SD-24 in docs/AUDIT_DEBT.md. That row also records two process
# failures in the entry this replaces, both introduced by #781: it was labelled
# `SD-23`, colliding with an unrelated and already-resolved SD-23, and it never
# got an AUDIT_DEBT row at all — so a live suppression carried no traceable
# rationale, which is exactly what the `SD-*` rule exists to prevent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SD-22: brace-expansion CVE-2026-14257 (HIGH, DoS via crafted brace patterns).
#
# Unrelated to the pnpm findings above, and NOT cleared by the pnpm upgrade:
# this copy comes from **our own** dependency tree, not from pnpm's bundle. The
# fix exists only in 5.0.8, whose `@isaacs` rewrite changed the module export
# from `module.exports = expand` to a named export; the maintainer did not
# backport to the function-export line, which `minimatch@3.1.5` requires and
# which ESLint and jest coverage pin. Forcing those onto 5.0.8 throws
# `TypeError: expand is not a function`. Full rationale in `.trivyignore` under
# SD-22 — repeated here because the two files do not share entries.
CVE-2026-14257
